">fifo</code> with four places, empty at the start. <code class=\"nobreak\">count</code> is not drawn. Here values often go in and come out at the same edge. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">out_valid</code> for every cycle.","explanationHtml":"<p>At cycle 1's edge a value goes in; none could come out of an empty FIFO. At cycle 2's one goes in and one comes out: one still waits. At cycle 3's the last comes out: 0. At cycle 4's one goes in, at cycle 5's one in and one out, at cycle 6's one in while the sink is not ready: two wait. They come out at the edges of cycles 7 and 8, so <code class=\"nobreak\">out_valid</code> is 0 again in cycle 8.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"fifo-both","source":"hdl/level-10/fifo/fifo_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"cycle","cycles":9,"signals":[{"label":"clk","path":"fifo_tb.clk","width":1,"role":"clock","changes":[[0,"1"],[0.5,"0"],[1,"1"],[1.5,"0"],[2,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3,"1"],[3.5,"0"],[4,"1"],[4.5,"0"],[5,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[7,"1"],[7.5,"0"],[8,"1"],[8.5,"0"]]},{"label":"in_valid","path":"fifo_tb.in_valid","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[0.5,"1"],[2.5,"0"],[3.5,"1"],[6.5,"0"],[8.5,"1"]]},{"label":"out_ready","path":"fifo_tb.out_ready","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[5.5,"0"],[6.5,"1"],[8.5,"0"]]},{"label":"out_valid","path":"fifo_tb.out_valid","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[3,"0"],[4,"1"],[8,"0"]],"samples":["0","1","1","0","1","1","1","1","0"]}]},"answer":"out_valid"},{"id":"fifo-fill-count","itemId":"fifo","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">push</code> is 1 at an edge where a value goes into <code class=\"nobreak\">fifo</code>, and <code class=\"nobreak\">pop</code> at one where a value comes out. Fill in when <code class=\"nobreak\">count</code> goes up by 1.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>push &amp; ~pop</code>: a value goes in and none comes out. When both happen at one edge, one in and one out, the count stays as 